WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:03.503
When we think about truth 
and justice and what that

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.172
actually means and what 
we're actually exploring 

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.341
in this show, it's not static.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.969
What justice looks like to you will 
not be what justice looks like to me.

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:14.222
I think we explore that 
beautifully in season three.

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:15.432
Do you have a lead?

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:16.349
Maybe.

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:17.017
Can I come with?

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.352
I play Eva Pierre, a 
high school principal 

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.439
where a number of her 
students are being trafficked. 

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.983
Over the course of the 
season layers are peeled back.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.776
I need to do more.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:30.530
The way I was able to get into the 
character is I lived it, unfortunately.

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:34.659
 I've had 30 years to intimately 
understand sexual violence

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:36.327
against young black and brown girls.

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:41.124
Eva is trying to heal and make 
amends and prove to herself

00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:43.126
and the world that 
she is a good person.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:47.172
I found my moments of justice 
and my version of the truth,

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:49.215
and I tried to give that to Eva.

